Draft body:
Hi Iris,

I wanted to share a quick update from the cooking class I took last night with Chef Maria. We learned to make fresh pasta from scratch (kneading, resting, and rolling the dough thin) and a rich Bolognese sauce to go with it. Chef Maria shared a few great tips for perfect pasta texture: use a mix of flours (00 or all-purpose with a bit of semolina), hydrate the dough just enough, knead until smooth and elastic, and let it rest before rolling and cutting — tagliatelle or pappardelle work great.

For the Bolognese, we built flavor starting with a slow-sweated soffritto, browned a mix of beef and pork, deglazed with wine, then simmered gently with tomato, a splash of milk, and plenty of time to develop depth.

It turned out fantastic — I’d love to make it for you sometime or share the recipe if you want.

Best,

